    {h:'Administration',items:['Subas (provinces) → Sarkar → Pargana → Village hierarchy','<b>Mansabdari system</b> (Akbar) — numerical rank (mansab): Zat (personal rank/salary) + Sawar (cavalry obligation)','<b>Zabt system</b> (Todar Mal) — measured land; classified quality; fixed revenue on 10-year average yield','Imperial atelier (karkhana) — Hamzanama (1400 illustrations under Akbar); Ustad Mansur (Jahangir)']},
    {h:'Art, Culture & Decline',items:['Bhakti saints: Kabir, Mirabai, Tukaram, Chaitanya — vernacular devotion; challenged caste orthodoxy','Sufi orders: Chishti, Suhrawardi — dargahs as Hindu-Muslim cultural synthesis centres','<b>Tansen</b> — greatest vocalist in Indian history; one of Akbar\'s Navratnas','Rajput painting schools: Mewar, Bundi, Kishangarh — blended Mughal technique with indigenous sensibility','Maratha Confederacy under Shivaji challenged Mughal authority; 3rd Panipat (1761) weakened Marathas too → British paramountcy']}
