    {q:'The zabt revenue system was introduced by which Mughal finance minister?',opts:['Birbal','Todar Mal','Abul Fazl','Man Singh'],ans:1,exp:'Raja Todar Mal, Akbar\'s Finance Minister (Diwan), introduced the zabt (zabti) system — measuring cultivated land, classifying it by quality, and fixing annual revenue based on the average yield of the previous 10 years.',yr:'UPSC 2022'}
