    {q:'"Drain of Wealth" theory was propounded by:',opts:['Bal Gangadhar Tilak','Gopal Krishna Gokhale','Dadabhai Naoroji','Lala Lajpat Rai'],ans:2,exp:'Dadabhai Naoroji (Grand Old Man of India) propounded the Drain of Wealth theory in "Poverty and Un-British Rule in India" (1901). He calculated that Britain drained India of £200–300 million annually.',yr:'UPSC 2019'}
