    {q:'Direct Crown rule was established by which Act after 1857?',opts:['Indian Councils Act 1861','Government of India Act 1858','Regulating Act 1773','Pitts India Act 1784'],ans:1,exp:'The Government of India Act 1858 transferred power from the East India Company to the British Crown. A Secretary of State for India was created; India Council was formed; Queen Victoria became Empress of India in 1876.',yr:'UPSC 2018'}
