    {q:'Which Article imposes on the Centre the duty to protect states against internal disturbance?',opts:['Article 352','Article 355','Article 356','Article 360'],ans:1,exp:'Article 355 imposes a duty on the Union to protect every state against external aggression and internal disturbance, and to ensure that the government of every state is carried on in accordance with the Constitution.',yr:'UPSC 2018'}
