    {q:'How many biodiversity hotspots does India have, and how many exist worldwide (as of 2023)?',opts:['2 in India, 25 worldwide','4 in India, 36 worldwide','6 in India, 40 worldwide','3 in India, 30 worldwide'],ans:1,exp:'India has 4 biodiversity hotspots — Western Ghats & Sri Lanka, Eastern Himalayas (Indo-Burma), Sundaland (Nicobar Islands) — out of 36 hotspots recognised worldwide.',yr:'UPSC 2016'}
