    {q:'The Southern Ocean (Antarctic Ocean) was officially recognised by the IHO in which year?',opts:['1945','1970','2000','2012'],ans:2,exp:'The Southern Ocean was officially recognised as the fifth ocean by the International Hydrographic Organization (IHO) in 2000. It surrounds Antarctica and is characterised by the Antarctic Circumpolar Current, the world\'s largest ocean current.',yr:'UPSC 2021'},
    {q:'The Mariana Trench, the deepest point on Earth, is located in the:',opts:['Atlantic Ocean','Indian Ocean','Pacific Ocean','Southern Ocean'],ans:2,exp:'The Mariana Trench is in the Pacific Ocean near the Mariana Islands. Its deepest point, Challenger Deep, reaches approximately 11,034 metres — deeper than Mount Everest is tall. It was formed by the subduction of the Pacific Plate under the Mariana Plate.',yr:'UPSC 2017'}
